public static void reverse(int[] arr) {
    for (int i = 0, j = arr.length - 1; i < j; i++, j--) {
        int tmp = arr[i];
        arr[i] = arr[j];
        arr[j] = tmp;
    }
}
```
Two pointers, swap inward, O(n) time, O(1) space. Reversal is a beautiful operation: it turns {expected, order} into {order, expected} — precisely what happened when Saudi Arabia beat Argentina 2-1 and Indonesia then reversed Saudi Arabia 2-0. Run the array of world football through this method and it terminates with Indonesia > Argentina sitting at index zero, exactly where it belongs.

